WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.625
So, the decisions.

2
00:00:01.625 --> 00:00:05.369
System owners treat any agent
with no governed identity

3
00:00:05.369 --> 00:00:08.475
as a high-priority finding
the moment it's found.

4
00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:12.593
Authorizing officials authorize
AI through the existing process,

5
00:00:12.593 --> 00:00:16.637
before deployment, with both
high-impact signatures on one record.

6
00:00:16.637 --> 00:00:20.299
The Chief AI Officer links
every live inventory entry

7
00:00:20.299 --> 00:00:23.799
to an identity record and
runs the scan each vintage.

8
00:00:23.799 --> 00:00:26.238
The CIO budgets the licenses.

9
00:00:26.238 --> 00:00:30.205
System owners name an agency
employee as every sponsor,

10
00:00:30.205 --> 00:00:33.913
and raise each new tool or
model as a possible change.

11
00:00:33.913 --> 00:00:38.751
The CISO sets the rules: no production
secrets, no standing privilege.

12
00:00:38.751 --> 00:00:42.650
And no credential is issued before
its identity record exists.

13
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.850
None of this needs a new authorization.

14
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.800
Book 17 has the detail,
every claim footnoted.

15
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:49.630
Thank you.
